# =============================================================================
# Phase 9 — Cron entry for daily Mindleaf database backup.
#
# Deployment:
#   - deploy.sh copies this file to /etc/cron.d/mindleaf-backup with
#     chmod 644 (cron.d files must not be group-writable or world-writable,
#     else cron refuses to install them).
#
# Cadence: 07:00 WIB daily. CRON_TZ is explicit because the VPS timezone
# (Asia/Shanghai) is not the application owner's timezone (Asia/Jakarta).
#
# Telegram is alert-only: the dump remains in R2 and Telegram is contacted
# only when the backup or retention step reports an anomaly. Configure
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN and TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID in /opt/mindleaf/.env.
#
# Log destinations:
#   - stdout → /var/log/mindleaf-backup.log (rotated by syslog)
#   - MAILTO is optional; if your VPS has a mail relay configured,
#     failures will email you. Empty MAILTO disables mail.
# =============================================================================
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
CRON_TZ=Asia/Jakarta
MAILTO=""

0 7 * * *  mindleaf  INSTALL_ROOT=/opt/mindleaf /opt/mindleaf/deploy/scripts/backup.sh >> /var/log/mindleaf-backup.log 2>&1
